{"run_id": "twenty_pr21506|A5|r2", "reason": "harness bug: graphify 0.9.108 query_graph resolves project_path to <project>/graphify-out/graph.json; the graph was served from outside the workspace, so the call failed (graph.json not found). Fixed by placing the graph at the standard location (competitor-servers.ts graphInWorkspace).", "invalidated_at": "2026-11-14T13:10+05:30", "record": {"run_id": "twenty_pr21506|A5|r2", "task_id": "twenty_pr21506", "arm": "A5", "backend": "graphify", "repeat": 2, "attempt": 1, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "effort": "high", "repo": "L", "split": "test", "task_type": "bug_localisation", "strata": {"difficulty": "medium", "lexical_overlap": "low", "indirect_boundary": "none", "gt_files": 1, "communities_spanned": 1, "gt_path_length": 0, "locality": "local"}, "status": "submitted", "turns": 54, "tool_calls": {"mcp__graphify__query_graph": 1, "Grep": 20, "Read": 28, "Bash": 1, "Glob": 2}, "retrieval_calls": 1, "usage": {"input": 64, "output": 22118, "cache_read": 1487240, "cache_write": 100930}, "total_tokens": 1610352, "cost_reported_usd": 0.05648692000000001, "cost_list_usd": 0.0461238, "cost_ledger_usd": 0.05648692000000001, "wall_ms": 126768, "api_ms": 118251, "tool_log": {"calls": 0, "result_tokens": 0, "errors": 0, "latency_ms": 0}, "files_read": 24, "answer": {"summary": "Root cause: ENUM_FILTER_OPERATORS (used for SELECT and RATING fields) omits the ordering operators gt/gte/lt/lte. The GraphQL schema still exposes them on enum filters (createGqlEnumFilterType adds gt/gte/lt/lte), and the unit specs expect SELECT to allow them, but the validator rejects them. So a prev/next request that compares the sort field with lt/gt (what in-app navigation from a SELECT-sorted index sends) fails at FilterArgProcessorService.process with \"Invalid filter : Operator \"lt\" is not valid for this \"severity\" SELECT field\". A hard reload sends no sort-based comparison, so it works. The fix is to add gt, gte, lt, lte to ENUM_FILTER_OPERATORS. C